Tropico 4 is the last (at this time) good Tropico game:
1. it keeps the simulation at a decent level and you can build some sort of plausible economy;
2. it keeps the jokes funny even when you played it for 50 hours;
3. it has a very nice soundtrack.
If you want to play as the dictator on your little tropical island, buy it. Avoid Tropico 5 and the "sour taste" of poorly scripted scenarios and jokes.

This is one of the most perfectly crafted games ever created in the industry's history. The amount of hours I have played this game on steam do not fully represent just how much I have played and loved this game in the past.
Dawn of War - and its following sequels - are Real Time Strategy done right. Almost perfectly right.
It has depth, whilst not being overly complex;
It stays passionately true to the lore where it can, whilst compromising on unit abilities/roles in clever ways;
It is functional, practical and is shipped with a wealth of features;
It has a rich story based campaign, reasonably accurate to lore, with entirely new plotlines being introduced in the later sequels;
Each race/unit is beautifully rendered in their [almost!] full glory and scale, with a graphical engine that still holds up even today;
It supports local and [formerly] online multiplayer, usually with relative ease;
$12.49 is a bargain for this calibre of game on Steam, not to mention that you get Imperial Guard bundled.
Even though you may be as excited as I am for the release of DOW3, if you haven't given this a shot yet you definately should. There is a lot of fun to be had with these titles, especially with a good LAN session.
9.8/10

I swear this game was not even tested for quality, just something thrown up for quick money.
Pros:
Cheap;
Looks promising;
Probably will make other indies feel better about their game;
A random light in front of your gun;
A good nerve ticker.
Cons:
First mistake I seen is right on launch, assuming where a monitor is positioned;
No instructions before "playing";
No in game pausing;
Discusting camera angles;
Poor mechanics;
Cars spawned inside walls (I hope it doesnt represent a car crash?);
Random signs falling from the sky (new wave);
Biker can drive through objects;
Rounds seemingly go through the Biker;
Auto zooming to p*** people off (no control), literally had it zoomed to my feet;
Times in which I walked the map with no enemy spawns;
Item menus are off, I can click AR and get shotty;
Shadows (if you call it that) are horrible;
The list can go on.
I personally never had resource hogging issues like some users.
Game is not worth its price, get it on a discount (much less than $0.50 CND).
Lastly, its better to have a few things working very well, then a bunch of non working features for show.
